# Bounded whole-V3 combination: implementation handoff — 22 October 2026

Source checkout: `/Volumes/Depot/Developer/glyph/.cache/held-rerun-20261019/repo`, branch `experiments/held-v3-single-owner-20261022`, base HEAD `83ccb82314f84449aa14c269f09b0da43cf65e2e`. The base preserves product `dec7509b3a18b2d71e27de023419f45c32fb10e7` plus reviewed verification and harness changes. Original V3 source is still `experiments/held-dense-frontier-v3-native-gated-20261021` / `aac036f938fbeff63c4b2dfe74dd781205c2b14f`, and `v3-original.patch` hashes to `02e2d697cf08f95abee99170abc47b71012f5653ba31ab21e7a7bcfffa7ca2b6`.

## Source and deletion map

The exact archived four-file V3 patch applied cleanly in the current isolated checkout, without resetting or overwriting the single-owner wave. `engine/state.rs` adds full-frontier admission before the existing sparse retained gather. The admission requires exact active owner/order coverage, contiguous prior source and record ranges, equal old/new source counts, no active or committed decorations, full or empty unpublished intervals where present, and the expected source end. It selects one `0..end` rope range only when every predicate passes. The existing owner-range path handles every declined admission; replacement/count-change and fresh paths are unchanged. The current complete-replacement preflight, pending-before-unpublished commit/ack order, and source-root restoration remain intact.

`engine/codec_gather.rs` adds the full-range iterator mode to the same `update_ordered_ranges` tree traversal and keeps the same owner callback, Codec execution, Stop suffix fallback, and transactional old-source clone/restore. `engine/work_attribution.rs` and `engine/transport/bitmap_replay_auth.rs` add native fixture counters `gather_full_frontier_modes`, `gather_full_range_next_calls`, and `gather_owner_range_next_calls` alongside the current `publication_ack_only_visits` and `preflight_seeded_old_units`. There is no new Wasm ABI, public API, or second executor.

Current `PlannerState::paragraph` is a binary search over P paragraph records. The N-owner admission makes N lookups, costing O(N log P), and replaces the owner-range iterator's own lookup/dispatch pass; there is no demonstrated net N-lookup deletion. Both variants retain O(N log P + G) owner/source-row work plus the shared rope traversal, binding and Codec work. The counterfactual asks whether removed range-boundary mechanics exceed added admission checks in complete callbacks. No latency improvement is assumed.

`benches/labs/package/{batching,stress,prepared-operations}.bench.ts` add `@frontier` to exactly four benchmark names: rewrite 512 labels in one group, publish 1024 retained Text instances, 1000 labels first same-length scene publication, and 1 labels first set. Callback bodies are unchanged. `benches/scripts/support/package-labs-suite.mts` and the runner declaration register `frontier`; `benches/scripts/workflows.test.mts` adds one routing assertion.

## Proof map for reviewer and Luna

- Native full-frontier and cold bytes/order: `dense_inter_setter_publication_attributes_actual_work` in `engine/state.rs`; `full_frontier_of_1024_owners_matches_independent_cold_gather` in `engine/codec_gather.rs`. The state test now reads one pending replacement through measurement/layout inspection, creates a nonempty independent `copy_glyphs` plan, overwrites that owner twice before the single publication, and checks its detached payload and placement payload before and after publication. It retains the archived 1,024-owner full-range/zero-owner-range counters and accepted cold physical order, active Codec buffer, and placement-byte oracle.
- Native fallback, Stop, rollback and retry: `streamed_stop_names_the_owner_and_resumes_existing_suffix_gather`, `streamed_callback_failure_restores_source_owner_and_count_change_stops`, and `seeded_range_edits_match_cold_gather_through_abort_and_retry` in `engine/codec_gather.rs`; `inter_assignment_labs_discriminator_matches_cold_preparation_and_gather` in `engine/state.rs` covers scattered interval fallback. `preflight_complete_replacement_avoids_old_units_and_preserves_ordered_edits` and existing pending/unpublished, rejection/retry, ABI-byte and arena-offset tests should remain in the native/package gate.
- Public lifetime and downstream publication: `packages/glyph/tests/integration/text-mutation-span-alignment.test.mjs` has `same-length bound roundtrip keeps each prepared read and the first split independent` (measure, glyphs, caret, split, single scene publication and independent cold output). `packages/glyph/tests/integration/glyph-placements.test.mjs` has `pending split matches publication and retains its independent copy across later edits`. Run these with the package integration/Three renderer gate and authenticated native/Wasm artifacts.
- Suite identity: resolve `@frontier` to exactly those four names before timing. Then use the fixed-20 single-call, eight-block installed-package protocol and preserve every sample, identity, p50/p90/p95, and block distribution. The native counter fixture is not the timed Node fixture; the 1,024 native test has 10,240 source units, which are distinct from 9,216 rendered profile glyphs. Do not infer timed Node counter values from it.

For focused execution, run `glyph:shaper-tests` with the named Rust filters above, the package integration files named above, and the package Labs workflow routing test. Then run the configured full native/package checks, artifact/size/memory authentication and downstream renderer gate required by the selection note. Luna alone runs commands. No tests, formatters, builds, gates, benchmarks, or browser commands were run by the implementor.

## Remaining limit

No single test combines an actual failed renderer delivery with the new pending overwrite and split sequence. Failed delivery invalidates the derived root; the existing checkpoint/replay and seeded abort/retry oracles cover that transition separately. The source reviewer should decide whether this separation leaves a concrete gap before gates. The timed Wasm full-range admission path is also unobserved directly; source predicates, native counters, installed-package output and complete-callback timing must be reported as distinct evidence.
